---
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<section aria-label={`About ${SITE.name}`} class="mx-auto max-w-[90rem] px-5 pt-32 sm:px-10 lg:pt-44">
  <div class="w-[78%] max-w-[21rem] text-body leading-relaxed lg:ml-[33.333%] lg:w-auto lg:pl-14 lg:[&>*]:max-w-[21rem]">
    <p class="reveal font-medium text-ink">
      {SITE.name} is not a new distro. It is a few programs that sit on top of one you already trust.
    </p>
    <p class="reveal mt-5 text-soft" style="--d: 70ms">
      FormalSpec describes each machine in Starlark: packages, files, services and the distro underneath. One lockfile
      pins every version, so every machine that applies the same commit ends up with the same software.
    </p>
    <p class="reveal mt-5 text-soft" style="--d: 140ms">
      The installer puts that description on a new disk. NativeDesktop apps and FormalShell are what you see once it
      boots.
    </p>
    <p class="reveal mt-5 text-soft" style="--d: 210ms">
      All of it is early. Each section below says what has run on real hardware and what has not.
      <a class="link mt-3 block w-fit py-2 text-ink" href={SITE.github}>Browse the code on GitHub</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
